      "role": "user",
      "content": "Thanks, that's a good start, but it feels a little bit \"safe,\" you know? Like, it's a bit generic. For the satire to really work, the contrast in how they actually *speak* needs to be much more intense. \n\nCan you rewrite them? For the new resident, maybe make them sound a bit more \"highly educated/professional\" — you know, more polished and perhaps a bit condescending. And for the local, can you give them more \"authentic grit\"? I want their slang and dialect to feel very grounded in a specific street culture so the clash really hits home. Make it punchier.",
      "source": "evaluator"
    },
